---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "embed/prototypes/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{%- from "system/component.njk" import component -%}

<main class="px-4 py-6 md:px-8 md:py-10 max-w-6xl mx-auto">
  <h1 class="text-xl md:text-3xl font-serif mb-2">Embed prototypes</h1>
  <p class="mb-10 text-sm text-neutral-700">
    Static designs for embedding OA.Report figures on external sites. Figures for {{ embed_figures.org.name }}, from the live API on {{ embed_figures.source.retrieved | date("d LLL yyyy") }}.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="tile_heading" class="mb-16">
    <h2 id="tile_heading" class="text-lg md:text-2xl font-serif mb-1">1. Tile</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-neutral-700">Highlights one headline figure for one completed period, such as total preprints in 2025. Answers “what’s the number?”</p>
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-12 rounded-sm bg-neutral-100 px-6 py-12">
      {% for key in ["unique_publications_2025", "compliance_2025", "preprints_2025", "das_2025"] %}
        {{ component("embed/tile", {
          figure: embed_figures.figures[key],
          org: embed_figures.org,
          asOf: embed_figures.source.retrieved,
          headingLevel: 3
        }) }}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="set_heading" class="mb-16">
    <h2 id="set_heading" class="text-lg md:text-2xl font-serif mb-1">2. Set</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-neutral-700">Shows one or two figures for a chosen period, each compared with an earlier period of the same length, such as this year so far against the same dates last year, or one full year against another. Answers “how does this period compare with the last?”</p>

    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-12 rounded-sm bg-neutral-100 px-6 py-12">
      {% for key in ["preprints_and_cc_by", "preprints_and_cc_by_share", "das"] %}
        {{ component("embed/set", {
          id: key,
          set: embed_figures.sets[key],
          org: embed_figures.org,
          asOf: embed_figures.source.retrieved,
          headingLevel: 3
        }) }}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="story_heading" class="mb-16">
    <h2 id="story_heading" class="text-lg md:text-2xl font-serif mb-1">3. Story</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-neutral-700">Shows how well a policy is working: a headline share or figure, with supporting figures, for a period since the policy, each compared with a period before it. Answers “is the policy working?”</p>
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-12 rounded-sm bg-neutral-100 px-6 py-12">
      {% for key in ["open_without_apcs", "policy_first_year", "apcs_and_preprinting", "apc_spend"] %}
        {{ component("embed/story", {
          id: key,
          story: embed_figures.stories[key],
          org: embed_figures.org,
          asOf: embed_figures.source.retrieved,
          headingLevel: 3
        }) }}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="trend_heading" class="mb-16">
    <h2 id="trend_heading" class="text-lg md:text-2xl font-serif mb-1">4. Trend</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-neutral-700">Shows how figures have moved over time: one or two metrics year by year, with the start of the policy marked. Answers “how has it changed over time?”</p>
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-12 rounded-sm bg-neutral-100 px-6 py-12">
      {% for key in ["free_vs_paid", "preprint_share"] %}
        {{ component("embed/trend", {
          id: key,
          trend: embed_figures.trends[key],
          org: embed_figures.org,
          asOf: embed_figures.source.retrieved,
          headingLevel: 3
        }) }}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
